Subject: Interpreter nursery: plain objects and small arrays are born young

What this does
  - The interpreter's construct handlers, object-literal templates, add-transition stores, own-slot stores and array literals (1..8 elements) allocate from the nursery chunks (negative count, no shape reference, edges uncounted). A young cell is promoted when anything can observe its count: a counted store into an old object, a shape update, a property add that needs the generic path, an element access through JS_ARR_VALS, a constant-folded literal kept in a constant pool, or a collection that finds it reachable.
  - JS_ARR_VALS promotes a young array; JS_ARR_VALS_RD is the raw read used by the interpreter's own element loads and by the collector. y_promote_cell and the young collection count and traverse array elements.
  - js_shape_prepare_update and convert_fast_array_to_array promote a young receiver; a cell promoted with count zero is parked like any object whose count reached zero.
  - The stack scan runs in a young-words-only mode when only the interpreter nursery is on. QJS_NONURSERY=1 turns the interpreter nursery off; it is on whether or not a unit is linked (every generated unit carries the young-cell forms).
  - The stack-scan vector is likewise owner-only: runtimes that do not own the nursery neither reset nor unpin it.

Why we need it
  Most interpreter-made objects and small arrays die within a few thousand allocations (earleyboyer 72%, deltablue 79%, pdfjs arrays 99%). A born-young cell costs no refcount traffic and no free; the plain interpreter gains 11% on earleyboyer, 5% on richards, 2.3x on an array-literal loop, with splay -3% and pdfjs -2%.

Soundness
  A young cell is reachable only from registers, other young cells and counted roots; the collector marks from the recorded roots and the pinned stack words, promotes what is reachable and drops the rest. The differential corpus and QJS_Y_STRICT=1 on all thirteen rows are clean.

Failure modes
  A unit generated before this change has no young-cell forms and must be regenerated.
  Region code (typed loops) stores through a nursery receiver only after qjs_y_promote_v turned it into an ordinary object.

